[[:db/retract 17592186193324 :question/answer-fields 17592186191871] {:db/id 17592186193324 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y<0\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/fc/fc71859cb4d1e58ea3d15c2da66bce014898281fe237f2e0c2396f96c84c9e79.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/ef/eff037b96b6a42120fdfa112a98d1e0749cdd56bd89acd647db448b08d7323ad.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,-1<y<0\\,\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186278573 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\nII. $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n\nIII. $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186278580 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4y>{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n\nII. $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A$\n\nIII. $∂A⊂A$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281306 :question/problem "![](images/6d/6debac35386e085a0197cf9eb3f2da65cc719ace67163cad625f58c056fb8f67.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/c0/c0b805c707981b9b6fcfa2ed387ad32a024fc845e6fd355a4b751ede4ad6a97e.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/69/69708aa698c38f8a29d3eb69083f893fd8fca183bd713387456624fc38b86fe9.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<x<2,\\text{ }0<y<2\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-f8eec0d0-f78f-5fc0-b443-6a20c34d9a4c" :activity/id #uuid "f8eec0d0-f78f-5fc0-b443-6a20c34d9a4c" :activity/title "Interiors and Boundaries of Sets" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048621 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-ca759e97-85ee-514a-bb82-190c512bf87c" "step-dab0e3df-3979-5bc3-b20c-cb2469721525" "step-c2cf7678-3eef-5b44-a81e-730e7364aaf8" "step-909e433a-8b41-5a26-89ce-2bbce68c19cf" "step-cd888233-2b60-5220-b469-4008e301268f"] :activity/first-step "step-ca759e97-85ee-514a-bb82-190c512bf87c" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-ca759e97-85ee-514a-bb82-190c512bf87c" :step/id #uuid "ca759e97-85ee-514a-bb82-190c512bf87c" :step/content 17592186193324 :step/next "step-dab0e3df-3979-5bc3-b20c-cb2469721525" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-dab0e3df-3979-5bc3-b20c-cb2469721525" :step/id #uuid "dab0e3df-3979-5bc3-b20c-cb2469721525" :step/content 17592186278573 :step/next "step-c2cf7678-3eef-5b44-a81e-730e7364aaf8" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {: